WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:07.770
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.360
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.320
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.030
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:23.370
Kana

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:23.710
Chiaki

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.500
Haruka

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.040
Many Faces

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:04.850
Delicious!

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.850
Really?

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.810
There's still more.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.480
I'll have some on rice, please!

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.940
Haruka. Everything is delicious to this fellow.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.990
What do you mean by that?

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.120
Do you have something to say about my rice bran with pickles?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.950
Yup! Apologize!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.160
I'm sorry!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.380
Besides, what's with these clothes?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.880
Where did you get them?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.630
I tried my best... I bought them at the supermarket!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.180
Chiaki. People change, don't they?

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.770
You know, I freed her from her heavy armor.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.780
And she began to walk on her own.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:02.530
I merely prepared her for her journey, and it gives me joy.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.830
Chiaki, whenever you feel like it,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.580
I'll prepare you a set of clothes that'll make you grin from ear to ear!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.000
<b>Volume 7
Madam Bakyura
"A scientist as well as a wife"
The Life of a Lovable Dumbass
The World's Greatest People - A Thin Line</b>

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.460
When did you start ignoring me?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.710
When you got to the "heavy armor" part.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.760
Hey, Mako-chan, don't spread your legs too much.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.140
Don't show us funny things, okay?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.000
The Next Day

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.930
<i>I really want to help someone prepare for their "journey".</i>

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.680
<i>Chiaki doesn't want to, so I'll have to find someone close to me...</i>

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.810
<i>I'll start with Keiko.</i>

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.480
<i>I have to take a good look at her face and decide what's appropriate for her...</i>

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.820
<i>But how should I make her take off her glasses?</i>

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.570
What's the matter, Kana?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.070
You have a stupid look on your face.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.240
Are you not feeling well?

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.030
I'm thinking about something!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.950
If you judge people by their looks, you'll get in trouble someday!

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.540
There are wolves in sheep's clothing and such.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.920
There was one in my home yesterday!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.420
I asked because I was worried about you.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.380
Ah, that's right. I just need to pretend to think intelligently.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.180
Keiko, lend me your glasses.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.100
Why?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:54.350
If I wear glasses while thinking, it'll make me look more intelligent.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.730
It makes you feel dizzy, doesn't it?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.490
What's wrong, Keiko? Are you feeling sleepy?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.080
No, I'm not.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.290
If you're sleepy, the infirmary has spare beds.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.540
I wonder about going to the infirmary just because I'm sleepy.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.300
Somehow my speech is becoming more intellectual!

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.880
I wonder about that.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.890
Okay, with this I can think intelligently.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.560
Now to think about how to make Keiko take off her glasses.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.890
What happened to your glasses?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.600
Minami-ke!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:40.150
<u>Founder</u>
Rice Sweets

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.650
I know that, Mom.
<u>Founder</u>
Rice Sweets

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:42.860
I know that, Mom.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.360
Someone is depending on me.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.740
I have to protect those three.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.910
Sir.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.660
I apologize for the inconvenience,

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.540
but please take your phone calls on the deck.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.040
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.970
Eh, well then,

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.640
To thank Chiaki's friends for always taking care of her,

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.810
I'm holding a class to teach you about self-defence!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.150
Roger!

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:29.320
Okay then, before I talk about mental safeguards...

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.700
I'm most worried about you, Uchida!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.700
Your concern is unnecessary!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.710
If a mister you don't know asks you to come along with him, do you go or not?

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:39.670
Not go!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.420
I'll give you sweets, so come along with me.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.710
I'll give you 10,000 yen, so come along with me.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.130
Don't react to that!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.430
Listen carefully, all of you.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.390
Even if it's a hundred, or even a thousand bills with Fukuzawa-sensei's picture on them,

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.140
understand that you're worth much more than that.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.390
Okay, Yoshino.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:00.480
Yukichi
Fukuzawa
Okay, Yoshino.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:00.850
Fukuzawa
Yukichi

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.650
Suppose that a hundred Fukuzawa-sensei and a thousand Noguchi-sensei were to fight each other,

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.400
Hideyo
Noguchi

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.400
Suppose that a hundred Fukuzawa-sensei and a thousand Noguchi-sensei were to fight each other,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.730
Who would be stronger?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.190
They are equal.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.400
Apologize to both the sensei.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.240
Kana-sensei!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.870
Yes, what is it?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.540
Lately a mister I don't know approached me and talked to me...

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.870
but he could be someone I know.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:25.290
I think I know him, but maybe I don't, but maybe I do...

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.380
Stop!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.800
You're quick at creating a weird atmosphere!

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.590
I found a girl who's more insecure than Uchida.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.720
I get the idea.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:39.310
You just need a way to tell whether he's a stranger or not.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:40.850
Yes, right!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.480
Coming!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:50.110
It's going to be hard without observational skills as polished as mine,

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.950
but there's a way to make him spill the beans.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:52.950
Hi, Haruka-chan.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.910
Ah, Takeru-ojisan!

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.160
If you're dealing with a male, begin by asking him,

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.790
"Takeru-ojisan, I haven't seen you for two months. How are your organs after that?"

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:07.920
You can tell whether he's a suspicious person or not by observing his reaction.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.960
Hey, Kana, you said Takeru...

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.220
This place seems pretty lively today.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.220
These are the souvenirs from Nagoya.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.720
Thanks as always!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.310
Well then, let's practice!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:25.600
Takeru-ojisan, I haven't seen you for two months. How are your organs after that?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.230
Two months ago?

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.110
A "white" heart?

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:32.820
"Black" heart?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.860
Both?

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.870
To differentiate that, you'll need senses as sharp as mine.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:38.660
Huh?

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:44.460
We call Takeru "Ojisan, Ojisan", but how is he related to us?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.420
Haruka, Chiaki, how is Takeru related to us?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.380
"Grey"?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.180
"Black"?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.550
Suspicious person?

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.560
Suspicious person?!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.640
Restraint

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.940
Hey, all of you...

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.850
Please let me go.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:12.360
Yes. Is that so? Thank you very much!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.360
Well then.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.620
Mom's elder sister's son.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.370
Looks like he's our cousin.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.990
Is that information reliable?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:22.910
Yup!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.210
Huh? Then you aren't our uncle!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.330
Have you even forgotten that?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.960
If I remember correctly, Chiaki called you "Uncle something", so you became known as Ojisan.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.140
So you were the uncle who gave her ten thousand yen during New Years?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.850
Yup, yup.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.180
Or were you the uncle who gave five thousand yen?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.270
Listen up, Uchida.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.190
No matter many Higuchi-sensei bills there are,

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.940
it doesn't come close to what you're worth!

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.530
Anyway, I'm saved.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.160
Glad that you're cleared of your charges.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.660
The two of you have forgotten too, haven't you?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.410
Minami-ke.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.170
Who would have thought that even Sensei would get amnesia.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.460
Oh no! Sensei and Ninomiya-san are gone!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.220
Sensei! Ninomiya-kun!

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.640
Not another car!

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.100
Don't! Sensei!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.440
Don't come over here!

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.860
Stop!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.360
Sensei and Ninomiya-kun.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.570
Look forward to it again next week.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.280
What?! Knocked down by a car again?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:47.370
Haruka-neesama. This reuse of plot devices must be due to corner-cutting.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.080
Please make a call to protest.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.980
Fujioka, what are you doing in the library?

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.490
I read books once in a while too.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.200
Same goes for you, Minami.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.530
I'm an avid reader, okay? Don't take me for an idiot!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:29.620
You're the Big Boss, so isn't being in this kind of place bad for appearances?

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.580
I've always wanted to ask,

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.040
Why do you always call me "Boss"?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.880
Hey Yuu, there seems to be a "Boss" other than you!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.840
I don't remember calling myself that.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.260
He can have that title if he wants.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.680
Hey Fujioka, seems that there's another Boss in this school besides you.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.940
Both of you are in year two, right?

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.780
Then you probably don't know of this.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.530
Two years ago when we were still first-year students,

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.990
There was a legendary person who was labeled as the Big Boss.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:12.960
Because of that, both last year and this year, someone was chosen to be the Boss.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:15.540
And she is the third-generation.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.130
Stop that.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.720
The first-generation didn't refer to herself as one, so there's no need to choose a person every year, right?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.880
The Boss is decided by a majority vote.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:26.600
Was the first-generation a nice person?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:29.010
Nice person?

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.020
Perhaps calling her weird would be more appropriate.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.070
She left behind numerous legends with her unpredictable behavior,

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.570
and she gradually became known as the Big Boss before she graduated and left.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.910
Minami Haruka-senpai!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.660
She broke all the glass windows in the school building...

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.750
It was the opposite, wasn't it?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.460
She wiped them all sparkling clean.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.330
She beat the crap out of a bunch of rowdy guys.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.920
She didn't beat them up, she rejected them.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.680
Keiko, lend me your notebook almost like you're giving it to me!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.770
I'll lend it to you, just keep quiet!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.480
What other legends were there?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.730
I'll write everything down for you.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.480
Thank you very much!

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.940
Don't dramatize it.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.690
I know.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.910
A few minutes later

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.040
I understand everything now.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.830
For the Big Boss, there can only be one, right?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.040
I'm telling you, I'll gladly give him the name.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.170
A title match would make everyone satisfied, won't it?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.760
Sounds interesting!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.680
Are you saying we should fight it out?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.430
How about deciding the winner with Rock, Paper, Scissors?

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.310
Erm... you, what's your name?

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.770
I'm Fujioka.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.690
Fujioka-kun...

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:03.980
Since I'm the Big Boss, a match usually means a fight.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:08.450
I might have forgotten how to play Rock, Paper, Scissors.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:13.410
Meaning that I may forget how to make a scissors,

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.370
And so I might be a bit late in showing my hand.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.330
Do you understand what I'm trying to say?

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.250
Yes, I do.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:25.960
Rock, Paper...

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:26.840
Scissors.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:27.840
Hey.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.760
Oh man, I lost!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.900
You. Are weak.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.070
I'm leaving the rest to you, Fujioka-kun.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.780
Okay...

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.950
By the way, what's your name?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.570
I'm Minami Kana.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:55.580
The younger sister of the legendary Big Boss.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.870
Is the legend... still...

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.290
Every day is a legend!

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.590
I didn't want to ruin their dreams.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:22.770
The book you're looking for isn't in our library either.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.230
But I found another interesting book instead.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:29.570
You reading a book? That's rare.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.700
Chiaki, help me with the dishes.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:36.910
Poured water from a flower vase on a Math teacher who sexually harassed her.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.500
Kana?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.000
Kakeru: Can mean both "pour" and "multiply"
"Poured" when used with a Math teacher could mean something else.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.210
And how many significant digits did you reach?
Kakeru: Can mean both "pour" and "multiply"

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:48.670
Hey Kana, let's have a little chat.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.510
Come over here.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.220
<b>The Legend of Minami Haruka</b>

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.060
Minami-ke.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.530
2 Years Earlier

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.030
I got the latest scoop on the Big Boss!

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.290
Not like I wanted it.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:22.120
Nah, you have to know this for the sake of your future.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.830
What do you mean by that?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.250
There, there.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.750
Today's topic is,

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:31.260
"Pouring water from the flower vase on the Math teacher who sexually harassed her".

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.840
A legend which happened only yesterday, hot off the press!

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:39.180
I'm sure it's just an exaggeration, with a few minor additions, right?

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.140
Okay.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.850
I won't say anything then.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.480
Interested?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.780
One day before that

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.780
Big Boss!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:00.240
I got new chalk!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.960
Hey, didn't I tell you to stop calling me that?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.750
About time you give up?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.380
No!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.550
Big Boss!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.630
Group 4 should be throwing out the rubbish today, right?

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.510
Isn't it Group 3, Big Boss?

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:17.220
Big Boss, when should the water in the vase be changed?

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.310
Everybody has decided on that name anyway.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:26.230
It means the head of an organization. That's no different from a class rep, right?

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:27.980
It's totally different!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.190
Big Boss, it's Group 4?

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.440
Group 3 right, Big Boss?

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.950
What about the water in the vase? Big Boss.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.240
I'll throw out the rubbish later!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.530
The water has already been changed!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.080
Roger that!

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.790
Well, I can't say you don't act like a Boss.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.210
This is how a class rep should behave!

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.220
Using the correct term is a bother anyway...

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.590
What's a bother?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.600
When a junior comes and asks, "What kind of person is the Big Boss?",

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:06.020
correcting each of them with "That's not the Big Boss, that's the class rep",

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.650
that's too troublesome.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.360
Yup, yup! They come pretty often!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.280
Tell them there's no Big Boss!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:19.280
But obviously they came to see you after they heard the Haruka legends.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.950
Aren't most of those false rumors?

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.660
But half of them are real, aren't they?

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.710
Who cares? As long as you are the Big Boss,

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:34.000
all the troublesome matters are gone, and the actual situation doesn't change much either.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.260
"Big Boss" sounds so cool! Just be one!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.600
Hey, Minami.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.650
Yes?

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:55.070
You came at the right time. I have something to ask you.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.030
What is it?

00:18:58.530 --> 00:18:59.820
Well, you see.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:05.990
Lately, after putting together what I heard from the teachers and students,

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.580
it appears that we have a gang boss in our class.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.960
Yeah, that's right. What a shock.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.170
I detest the use of violence!

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:21.390
The person who calls himself the Big Boss is a scum of society!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:28.810
That's why I want you, the class rep, to help me look for the Big Boss.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.520
Of course, you just need to give me any information regarding the Big Boss in secret.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.110
Because if the Big Boss notices you, you'll be in deep trouble.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.280
But...

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.190
What's wrong?

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:42.950
Even among gang bosses, I think there are different kinds.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.200
And this person might have become one even if they didn't want to.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.370
That won't do!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:53.080
Because you're both students... and also in the same class,

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.630
I understand you'd like to cover up for him.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.550
Especially you, Minami, you're too kind of a person.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:01.930
But think about those students who are crying because of him.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:05.850
I don't think there are any crying students...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.970
I said that won't do!

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:12.100
Minami, you're too kind.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.350
I also understand why you want to believe that.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:17.860
<i>It's hopeless... I must change the subject somehow...</i>

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:19.860
<b>Find your partner! The red thread</b>

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.450
<b>tying you to your destiny!
Find your partner! The red thread</b>

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:26.160
Sensei! You're getting married soon, aren't you?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.040
I know how to read palms.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.750
You'll meet your destined partner within this week!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:41.800
<i>I guess I'm pushing it a little?</i>

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.260
Is that so?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.890
Finally it's my turn to get married?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.770
Well, I've been thinking that it's about time!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.940
So, how old is she?

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.150
Is she a beauty? Don't tell me she's a celebrity?!

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.400
Or maybe even from Hollywood?!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.910
The flower has wilted!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.370
I'll go throw it away!

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.370
No need, no need! You don't need to!

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.160
Minami, you're so kind.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.500
Forget about that, take a better look at my palm-

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.460
No!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.340
You have to pay attention to these little details.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.670
You can never tell when your destined partner is looking!

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:25.220
You... You're right.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:27.090
Ah, there you are.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.760
The dustbin isn't in the classroom, Big Boss.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.400
There it is.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.560
Right here.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.570
I overheard this.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:50.530
There's some legendary boss in the junior high school!

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.240
Absurd.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:55.790
Things such as legends or mythical creatures are relics of the bygone Showa Period.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.960
You know some difficult words!

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:31.760
Next Episode

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.550
How's that Fujioka doing lately?
Next Episode

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:34.100
How's that Fujioka doing lately?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.970
That guy became the fourth-generation Big Boss.

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.180
You and the Big Boss are ganging up against me!

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:39.560
Next Time, Hosaka.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:40.690
Hosaka
Next Time, Hosaka.

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:43.230
Fujioka must be tired of dealing with an idiot.
Hosaka

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.570
By the way, what's a Hosaka?
Hosaka

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:46.020
Hosaka
